WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.469
Joining us now, basketball legend, NBA

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:04.671
analyst Mr. Charles Barkley.

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:06.172
Good morning to you, sir.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:08.808
Really appreciate you joining us.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:10.143
Of course, Don.

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:10.610
Thank you.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.145
Thank you guys for having me.

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:13.513
Why so outspoken,

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:15.148
especially when it comes to this issue?

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:15.782
You know,

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:16.750
even as someone

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.151
who is you're covering sports

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:18.952
but you're speaking out

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:19.686
about issues

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:22.856
that have to do with culture and society,

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:25.592
why so outspoken about this?

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:28.194
Well, I don't

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.729
I don't like that word outspoken

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:33.099
because I hope anybody who sees racism

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:36.169
in any form whatsoever, just stand up,

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:37.203
whether

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:38.505
it's a black person,

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:40.840
a Hispanic person, a Jewish person

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.108
or Asian, Asian, he's

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:43.410
going a big deal in this country

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:44.110
right now.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.979
So anybody

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:47.580
should try to do the right thing.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.382
If you see something wrong

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:50.817
when it comes to race

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:52.952
are homophobic or sexist,

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:54.821
you should always say something.

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:56.523
So and I'm always going to do that.

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:58.391
I don't care about the repercussions.

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:00.627
If I see something wrong happening, Don,

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:03.063
I'm going to say something.

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.831
How do you think the league

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:05.565
should deal with it?

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:05.999
Because,

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:08.068
listen, he's still on suspension,

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:08.635
but how do you think

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:09.769
the league should deal with it?

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.871
The reason I ask is because, you know,

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:13.473
everyone is speaking out about it.

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:15.141
Kyrie Irving is facing you know,

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:16.976
what he's facing.

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:17.944
But the league let him go

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:19.612
for a long time.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:20.980
They they sort of

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.315
are forcing him to apologize.

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.084
But would it these are his real beliefs.

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:26.252
Should they be dealing with that as well?

00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:27.153
Maybe they have someone

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:28.788
who actually believes these things.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:29.722
I'm not saying it's right

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:31.691
instead of forcing him to apologize.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.326
Maybe they should be dealing with that.

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:33.960
That part of it

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:38.531
I said that's a great question, Don.

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.800
Don, people have the right to feel

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:41.668
and say what they want.

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:43.136
Do we have freedom of speech?

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:44.370
But they are repercussions

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.473
when you say certain things.

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:48.241
Listen, I don't know Kyrie Irving.

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.409
I don't know if he's a good guy

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:50.477
or a bad guy.

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:52.145
I think he's been suspended,

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:53.046
rightfully so.

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:54.114
And I think he should come back

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:55.682
and play in the NBA.

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:56.616
But, you know,

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:58.418
that's a really slippery slope

00:01:58.418 --> 00:01:59.319
because, you know,

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:00.420
people always talk about

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.621
freedom of speech,

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:03.790
freedom of affect,

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.592
or you say whatever you want to.

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:07.227
But there are repercussions.

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:07.594
I mean,

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:09.496
and he's he's paying for that right now.

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:11.231
But this time with free speech

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:12.966
is really gotten out of hand.

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:15.034
I mean, you just can't go around

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:15.635
and salt

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:16.503
and people

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:17.570
and think it's okay

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.572
just because it's freedom of speech.

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:20.740
Well, people say, well, listen,

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:21.875
if I don't get to say what I say,

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:22.709
it's cancel culture.

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:23.843
And I don't know if you

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.411
you probably do not agree with that.

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:31.251
You know, I'm not I'm I don't

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:33.186
like to use the term cancel culture

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:34.287
because I don't want anybody

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:35.822
council counsel.

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.824
But you should be called to the carpet

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:39.626
if you said something wrong.

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.461
No, I don't believe somebody should

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:43.663
lose their job or things like that.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.599
But you just you should be called out

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.034
if you said something stupid.

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:49.068
Hey, I've been called out

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:51.104
minutes and I have no problem with that.

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:53.173
But I hate the term cancel culture

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:55.241
because very few people are canceled.

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:57.243
Let's be honest and realistic

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:58.545
Yeah, that's a that's a good point.

00:02:58.545 --> 00:02:59.279
Can I something real quick

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:00.280
that I didn't think to do?

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:00.947
Maybe you didn't see it

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:01.981
so you might not be able to answer.

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:02.949
Did you see SNL?

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:05.518
Did you see Dave Chappelle, his monologue

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.556
I did not, but I listened.

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:10.490
Let me just say this.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:13.226
I'm a Dave Chappelle fan.

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:16.462
I have a really strict line on racism.

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:19.499
Sexism, homophobic, things like that.

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:21.334
Just wrong.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.036
It's nothing to joke about.

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:24.571
It's a very serious subject.

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:25.672
You know, Don, it's crazy.

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:27.974
I'm almost 60 years old

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:29.442
and I grew up in Alabama,

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:30.310
you know, and obviously

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.544
I know about Montgomery,

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:33.546
Selma, Birmingham and things like that.

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:34.581
To still be having

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:37.083
a racial conversation 60 years later,

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:38.751
and we're debating

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.553
whether people have the right to say it

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:43.289
and joke about it is really it makes

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:45.058
it just makes me sad, you know,

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:46.893
it makes me it makes me mad,

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.861
but it really just makes me sad

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:50.363
that 60 years later,

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:51.497
we're still saying

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:53.166
having a racial conversation

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:54.534
60 years later

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:56.202
and almost said Look, almost

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:57.971
more than a decade ago, I do have to say

00:03:57.971 --> 00:03:59.272
and then let you guys jump in here

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:00.873
because I want to hold this conversation.

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:02.742
One of the first people to contact me

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:05.845
after I came out was this man

00:04:06.613 --> 00:04:07.180
right here,

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.415
and that was over a decade ago.

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:10.016
So these issues

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:10.883
are really important to you

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.318
and you always stand up for

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:13.486
people's individual rights.

00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:17.724
Well, you know, Don, first of all,

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:19.626
one thing that always has disturbed me

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:20.493
as a black person,

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:21.761
which really bothers me

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:23.830
about the Kyrie Irving situation

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:26.266
and the Kanye West situation,

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:27.900
first of all, being black in America

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.003
is already hard enough.

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:32.405
And for us to go at other ethnic groups

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:33.906
just makes things worse

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.508
because it's hard enough being black.

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:37.143
And one thing is always disappointing me.

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:39.012
Black people treat gay people.

00:04:39.012 --> 00:04:40.413
We are the worst

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:42.382
when it comes to treating gay people.

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:43.850
And as one thing growing up,

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:45.818
it really always bothers me.

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:47.220
And I want to reach out to you

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:48.521
and all my gay friends,

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:50.290
all my transgender friends

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:50.990
and tell you, man,

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.026
I got no love and respect for you.

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:54.827
I want you to be you.

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:56.696
And I wanted you to know that that day,

00:04:56.696 --> 00:04:57.463
because I understand

00:04:57.463 --> 00:04:58.865
being black, what it's like being gay

00:04:58.865 --> 00:05:00.500
because you get mistreated

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.701
and it's really unfortunate

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:03.102
and sad and stupid, to be

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:03.803
honest with you.

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:06.005
Charles, you mentioned your home

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:06.739
